cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite this repository."
title: "LeFT: Learn, Freeze, and Transfer an Activation Function Across Architectures"
abstract: >-
  LeFT is a framework for learning a globally shared activation function inside
  a source network, freezing it, and transferring it to independently
  initialized target networks without transferring any source-network weights.
  This repository holds the framework, two activation implementations (FAct, a
  truncated Fourier series; PAU, a Pade rational function), the four target
  architectures, and the learned coefficient artifact behind the paper's
  results.
type: software
